#: ../../index.rst:5
msgid "Welcome to Spyder's Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:7
msgid "Screenshot of the Spyder main window, with the default panel layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:11
msgid "Spyder is a powerful scientific environment written in Python, for Python, and designed by and for scientists, engineers and data analysts. It features a unique combination of the advanced editing, analysis, debugging, and profiling functionality of a comprehensive development tool with the data exploration, interactive execution, deep inspection, and beautiful visualization capabilities of a scientific package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:22
msgid "Where to go now?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:24
msgid "Spyder's documentation provides a variety of resources that will help you learn how to use the application and explore each one of its panes. These include video tutorials, in-depth descriptions and how-to guides covering a wide range of needs and experience levels with Spyder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:38
msgid "If you are looking for a summary of its features and interface, check out the :ref:`tour`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:49
msgid "If you don't have Spyder installed and want to get started, follow the :ref:`install-guide`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:60
msgid "If you are completely new to Spyder, watch our basic tutorial series, :ref:`tutorials-beginner`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:71
msgid "If you are familiar with Spyder and want to explore the functionality of its panes in more detail, go to :ref:`panes-index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:82
msgid "If you've run into a Spyder problem and need help solving it, take a look at our :ref:`troubleshooting guide <troubleshooting-guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:93
msgid "If you have a question about Spyder, visit the :ref:`faq` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:103
msgid "Join our community"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:105
msgid "Spyder is open source software, which means that is free for everyone to use and anyone can contribute to it. We encourage everyone to become a part of our community and help develop Spyder!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:114
msgid "Looking to contribute your code?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:116
msgid "Spyder is written in the same Python language that you use it to develop, so its easy to get started contributing to it. You can follow our `contributing guide <contributing guide_>`__ to set up a development environment, and you can get involved with the project through our `Github repository <Github repository_>`__. The easiest way to get started is helping us resolve items on our `issue tracker <issue tracker_>`__, either by fixing bugs in Spyder, or helping users troubleshoot their problems (which doesn't require writing any code)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:132
msgid "Want to help writing docs?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:134
msgid "We welcome your contributions of corrections, additions and enhancements to these docs. Check out the `docs contributing guide <docs contributing guide_>`__ to learn how to submit a PR with your changes on our `docs repo <docs repo_>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:147
msgid "Interested in translating Spyder?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:149
msgid "In order to reach more users around the world in need of a powerful scientific Python environment, we welcome your help translating the documentation and the interface into different languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:151
msgid "For this purpose we use `Crowdin <Crowdin_>`__, which provides a simple web based interface for translators, proofreaders and managers, so everyone can help us translate Spyder into any language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:161
msgid "Want to be part of our social media?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:163
msgid "Connect with Spyder through our social media channels to stay up to date with our current developments!"
msgstr ""
